+ <h1>Welcome to Little Browser</h1>
+ <p class="lead">A calm, private Chromium browser. No account to sign in to, no Google services
+  running in the background, and no search engine until you choose one.</p>
+
+ <section>
+  <h2>Spaces</h2>
+  <ul>
+   <li>A space is a set of tabs for one part of your life: work, home, a project.
+    Switch spaces with the icons at the bottom of the sidebar, <kbd>⌃1</kbd>…<kbd>⌃9</kbd>,
+    <kbd>⌃⌥←</kbd> / <kbd>⌃⌥→</kbd>, or a two-finger sideways swipe over the sidebar.</li>
+   <li><b>+</b> at the bottom of the sidebar creates a space. Right-click a space's icon to
+    rename or delete it.</li>
+   <li>Each space uses a <b>profile</b>: its own logins, cookies and history. Several spaces can
+    share one profile, or keep a client's logins apart in a profile of its own.</li>
+  </ul>
+ </section>
+
+ <section>
+  <h2>Getting around</h2>
+  <ul>
+   <li><kbd>⌘T</kbd> or <kbd>⌘L</kbd> opens the command bar: type an address or a search, find an
+    open tab or a page from your history, or run a command.</li>
+   <li>Quit and come back later: every window returns to its space with its tabs.</li>
+  </ul>
+ </section>
+
+ <section>
+  <h2>Privacy</h2>
+  <ul>
+   <li>Little Browser is built on <a href="https://github.com/ungoogled-software/ungoogled-chromium">ungoogled-chromium</a>:
+    Google sign-in, sync and background services are removed.</li>
+   <li>Searches go to the engine you picked. Change it in
+    <a href="chrome://settings/search" target="_self">Settings › Search engine</a>.</li>
+  </ul>
+ </section>
+
+ <section>
+  <h2>How to</h2>
+  <details><summary>Install and update extensions</summary>
+   <p>There's no Chrome Web Store button yet. The
+    <a href="https://github.com/NeverDecaf/chromium-web-store">chromium-web-store</a> extension adds one:</p>
+   <ol>
+    <li>Set <a href="chrome://flags/#extension-mime-request-handling" target="_self">extension-mime-request-handling</a>
+     to <code>Always prompt for install</code> and relaunch.</li>
+    <li>Open the extension's <a href="https://github.com/NeverDecaf/chromium-web-store/releases">releases page</a>
+     and click the latest <code>Chromium.Web.Store.crx</code>.</li>
+   </ol>
+   <p class="small">You can also <a href="https://ungoogled-software.github.io/ungoogled-chromium-wiki/faq#downloading-the-crx-file">install
+    extensions by hand</a>, but they won't update on their own.</p>
+  </details>
+  <details><summary>Turn on spellcheck</summary>
+   <p>Dictionaries aren't downloaded automatically, because that would contact Google.</p>
+   <ol>
+    <li>Open the <a href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/deps/hunspell_dictionaries/+/main">dictionary list</a>,
+     click the <code>.bdic</code> file for your language, then <b>txt</b> at the bottom right, and save it.</li>
+    <li>Choose that file here to convert it: <input id="bdic" type="file" accept=".txt,text/plain"></li>
+    <li>Move the converted <code>.bdic</code> into a <code>Dictionaries</code> folder next to your
+     profiles (<a href="chrome://version" target="_self">chrome://version</a> shows the Profile Path;
+     the folder goes one level up).</li>
+    <li>Turn spellcheck on in <a href="chrome://settings/languages" target="_self">Settings › Languages</a>.</li>
+   </ol>
+  </details>
+ </section>
+
+ <p class="small">This page is always at <a href="chrome://welcome" target="_self">chrome://welcome</a>.
+  More settings for power users are in <a href="chrome://flags" target="_self">chrome://flags</a>.</p>
+</main>
